id: pm-vae5ec
title: "Stateless MCP core: request-local version and capabilities, mandatory server/discover, typed result envelopes, and deterministic identity"
description: Implement the 2026-07-28 base protocol model in SDK-owned contracts and replace initialize-scoped behavior with per-request metadata and mandatory discovery.
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:mcp","area:sdk",protocol-negotiation,result-type,server-discover,stateless
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:08:17.895Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T05:08:17.895Z"
deadline: "2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "server/discover is mandatory and deterministic with exact supported versions, capabilities, extensions, and identity; Every request validates request-local protocol version and client capabilities and every result identifies the server; Unsupported versions, missing capabilities, malformed metadata, and header mismatches return the specified structured error codes; Ordinary results include resultType complete and compatibility treatment of omitted resultType is isolated and tested; No behavior depends on initialize or notifications/initialized state; The public pm SDK exposes transport-neutral negotiation, discovery, metadata validation, and result-envelope primitives"
goal: Standards-correct stateless MCP core
objective: Make every request self-describing and every server capability discoverable without connection-local initialization
value: "Hosts can negotiate, retry, load-balance, and cache safely across independent requests"
why_now: The current server hardcodes 2025-06-18 and retains initialize state that the 2026-07-28 core removes
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: critical
confidence: high
